{"schema_version":1,"seq":6,"event_id":"evt_20260525_043001_0006","run_id":"2026-05-25-each-worktree-owns-its-own-run-dir","at":"2026-05-25T04:30:01-04:00","actor":{"type":"agent","name":"timothy.shee"},"type":"AssumptionRecorded","status":"planning","payload":{"assumption_id":"ASM-001","text":"The two known orphan run dirs (`2026-05-24-fix-generated-lines-base-ref-head/`, `2026-05-24-token-efficiency-pass-2/`) have valid `metadata.target.worktree.path` pointing at existing worktrees on disk.","reason":"Both have completed their lifecycle and their worktrees were created normally by `/start` against the workbench monorepo path.","impact":"medium \u2014 if untrue, the migration script will fail loudly and need a manual fallback. Verify at build start.","source_artifact":"plan.md"}}
{"schema_version":1,"seq":7,"event_id":"evt_20260525_043001_0007","run_id":"2026-05-25-each-worktree-owns-its-own-run-dir","at":"2026-05-25T04:30:01-04:00","actor":{"type":"agent","name":"timothy.shee"},"type":"AssumptionRecorded","status":"planning","payload":{"assumption_id":"ASM-002","text":"`git worktree list --porcelain` lists every workbench worktree from any of its working copies, including master's.","reason":"All worktrees share the same `.git` admin directory; the porcelain output is consistent across CWDs.","impact":"high \u2014 `find_run`'s enumeration depends on this. Verify by running `git worktree list` from each worktree before relying on it.","source_artifact":"plan.md"}}
{"schema_version":1,"seq":8,"event_id":"evt_20260525_043001_0008","run_id":"2026-05-25-each-worktree-owns-its-own-run-dir","at":"2026-05-25T04:30:01-04:00","actor":{"type":"agent","name":"timothy.shee"},"type":"AssumptionRecorded","status":"planning","payload":{"assumption_id":"ASM-003","text":"`git worktree add -b <branch> <path> <base_ref>` is safe to run while the workbench is mid-tick (e.g. another CLI command is running). No global lock is needed beyond what `lib/locks.py` already provides per-run.","reason":"Today's `cmd_start` already calls this at human-driven cadence; no race observed.","impact":"low \u2014 even if a race exists, the failure mode is a `RepoError` on the second concurrent worktree add, which we already handle.","source_artifact":"plan.md"}}
{"schema_version":1,"seq":9,"event_id":"evt_20260525_043001_0009","run_id":"2026-05-25-each-worktree-owns-its-own-run-dir","at":"2026-05-25T04:30:01-04:00","actor":{"type":"agent","name":"timothy.shee"},"type":"AssumptionRecorded","status":"planning","payload":{"assumption_id":"ASM-004","text":"The workbench checkout path inside any worktree is at the same relative subpath as in master (`agentic-development-task-system-v3__ai/agent-workbench-live/`).","reason":"Worktrees are checkouts of the same monorepo; the workbench dir is part of the tracked tree.","impact":"high \u2014 A4's pre-merge commit depends on this. Verify by inspecting one of the existing worktrees.","source_artifact":"plan.md"}}
{"schema_version":1,"seq":10,"event_id":"evt_20260525_043001_0010","run_id":"2026-05-25-each-worktree-owns-its-own-run-dir","at":"2026-05-25T04:30:01-04:00","actor":{"type":"agent","name":"timothy.shee"},"type":"AssumptionRecorded","status":"planning","payload":{"assumption_id":"ASM-005","text":"Removing a worktree's run dir during `complete`/`abandon` is safe because the worktree itself is removed shortly after; nothing else holds a path into `runs/<id>/`.","reason":"Lifecycle ends here; no further reads after the merge.","impact":"low \u2014 defensive logging if a stale handle is somehow held.","source_artifact":"plan.md"}}
{"schema_version":1,"seq":11,"event_id":"evt_20260525_043001_0011","run_id":"2026-05-25-each-worktree-owns-its-own-run-dir","at":"2026-05-25T04:30:01-04:00","actor":{"type":"agent","name":"timothy.shee"},"type":"AssumptionRecorded","status":"planning","payload":{"assumption_id":"ASM-006","text":"The `agent-workbench-live/AGENTS.md` \"Source of truth\" section is the right place to record the new run-dir-location rule, and downstream tooling reads conventions from there.","reason":"Other lifecycle rules already live there.","impact":"low \u2014 cosmetic.","source_artifact":"plan.md"}}
{"schema_version":1,"seq":12,"event_id":"evt_20260525_043001_0012","run_id":"2026-05-25-each-worktree-owns-its-own-run-dir","at":"2026-05-25T04:30:01-04:00","actor":{"type":"agent","name":"timothy.shee"},"type":"AssumptionRecorded","status":"planning","payload":{"assumption_id":"ASM-007","text":"Existing tests in `tests/test_e2e.py` use a target repo distinct from `self.tmp` (the workbench), so today's behavior (run dir at `self.tmp / \"runs\" / run_id`) is correct for them and remains correct after this change.","reason":"`_repo()` returns a fresh tmp dir; `--repo-path` points there.","impact":"medium \u2014 if untrue, the existing assertions will fail and need rewrites. Confirmed by reading lines 50-65 and 120-139 of `test_e2e.py`.","source_artifact":"plan.md"}}
{"schema_version":1,"seq":13,"event_id":"evt_20260525_043001_0013","run_id":"2026-05-25-each-worktree-owns-its-own-run-dir","at":"2026-05-25T04:30:01-04:00","actor":{"type":"agent","name":"timothy.shee"},"type":"AssumptionRecorded","status":"planning","payload":{"assumption_id":"ASM-008","text":"For the new self-modifying E2E scenario, initializing `self.tmp` as a git repo (with `bin/` and `lib/` populated from `ROOT/`) plus a tracking commit will produce a valid workbench-as-target setup.","reason":"The only thing self-modifying needs is `cfg.root` to be inside `target.repo.path`. `self.tmp` is the workbench root; `--repo-path = self.tmp` makes that true.","impact":"medium \u2014 if `make_tmp_workbench` does something that breaks `git init`, the test scaffolding needs an adapter. Verify during C1 implementation.","source_artifact":"plan.md"}}
{"schema_version":1,"seq":14,"event_id":"evt_20260525_043001_0014","run_id":"2026-05-25-each-worktree-owns-its-own-run-dir","at":"2026-05-25T04:30:01-04:00","actor":{"type":"agent","name":"timothy.shee"},"type":"AssumptionRecorded","status":"planning","payload":{"assumption_id":"ASM-009","text":"No external CI / consumer depends on `runs/<id>/` paths in master's working tree being untracked.","reason":"They're untracked today; nothing references them. The merge-on-complete that already exists is the contract for \"runs eventually arrive on master via merge\".","impact":"low.","source_artifact":"plan.md"}}
{"schema_version":1,"seq":15,"event_id":"evt_20260525_043001_0015","run_id":"2026-05-25-each-worktree-owns-its-own-run-dir","at":"2026-05-25T04:30:01-04:00","actor":{"type":"agent","name":"timothy.shee"},"type":"AssumptionRecorded","status":"planning","payload":{"assumption_id":"ASM-010","text":"`lib/board/app.py` is the only file that schedules a watchdog observer; nothing else watches `cfg.runs_path` for filesystem events.","reason":"One observer in one place; grep confirms.","impact":"low.","source_artifact":"plan.md"}}
{"schema_version":1,"seq":16,"event_id":"evt_20260525_043001_0016","run_id":"2026-05-25-each-worktree-owns-its-own-run-dir","at":"2026-05-25T04:30:01-04:00","actor":{"type":"agent","name":"timothy.shee"},"type":"DecisionRecorded","status":"planning","payload":{"decision_id":"DR-001","decision":"Detect self-modifying runs (workbench is inside the target repo) via a runtime helper `runs.is_self_modifying(cfg, meta)`. Non-self-modifying runs keep today's \"run dir in `cfg.runs_path`\" behavior.","rationale":"The bug only manifests when the workbench IS the target repo's content. For unrelated product repos, the run dir lives in the workbench checkout's master and that's correct.","alternatives_considered":"(a) Always put the run dir inside the worktree, regardless of repo. (b) Always put it in master. (c) Add a config flag.","why_not_alternatives":"(a) would put run dirs in unrelated product worktrees, polluting their working trees and breaking the contract that workbench artifacts don't touch product repos. (b) is today's broken behavior. (c) adds knobs nobody needs to turn \u2014 the right answer is computable.","source_artifact":"plan.md"}}
{"schema_version":1,"seq":17,"event_id":"evt_20260525_043001_0017","run_id":"2026-05-25-each-worktree-owns-its-own-run-dir","at":"2026-05-25T04:30:01-04:00","actor":{"type":"agent","name":"timothy.shee"},"type":"DecisionRecorded","status":"planning","payload":{"decision_id":"DR-002","decision":"`find_run` is strict (raises on collision); `iter_all_runs` is permissive (prefers worktree, warns).","rationale":"Single-run mutations need certainty; the board needs to render even when on-disk state is messy.","alternatives_considered":"Always strict; always permissive.","why_not_alternatives":"Always strict breaks the board for cosmetic on-disk weirdness. Always permissive risks writing to the wrong copy in a transition.","source_artifact":"plan.md"}}
{"schema_version":1,"seq":18,"event_id":"evt_20260525_043001_0018","run_id":"2026-05-25-each-worktree-owns-its-own-run-dir","at":"2026-05-25T04:30:01-04:00","actor":{"type":"agent","name":"timothy.shee"},"type":"DecisionRecorded","status":"planning","payload":{"decision_id":"DR-003","decision":"`abandon` archives the run dir on master via a non-merge tree copy (`git read-tree` / `git archive`), NOT a `git merge` of the agent branch.","rationale":"Abandoning means the code work is discarded. Merging the agent branch would pull the work into master alongside the audit trail. Tree-copy isolates the run-dir delivery from the code-changes-delivery.","alternatives_considered":"Merge-then-revert; merge-into-subtree; pure metadata transition with no master delivery.","why_not_alternatives":"Merge-then-revert clutters history. Subtree merge is for external repos. Pure metadata is what we have today and the brief's acceptance criterion explicitly requires master to have the abandoned run dir.","source_artifact":"plan.md"}}
{"schema_version":1,"seq":19,"event_id":"evt_20260525_043001_0019","run_id":"2026-05-25-each-worktree-owns-its-own-run-dir","at":"2026-05-25T04:30:01-04:00","actor":{"type":"agent","name":"timothy.shee"},"type":"DecisionRecorded","status":"planning","payload":{"decision_id":"DR-004","decision":"The migration script (`tools/migrate_orphan_runs.py`) is run-then-deleted as part of this run's build phase. It is NOT committed permanently.","rationale":"One-shot tools that solve a one-time data state shouldn't live in the repo forever. The two known orphans are the only orphans; any future orphans should be impossible after A1 lands.","alternatives_considered":"Commit and keep; commit then delete in a follow-up; do the migration by hand.","why_not_alternatives":"Keeping it is rot. A separate follow-up is bookkeeping the build doesn't need. By-hand is fragile and undocumented.","source_artifact":"plan.md"}}
{"schema_version":1,"seq":20,"event_id":"evt_20260525_043001_0020","run_id":"2026-05-25-each-worktree-owns-its-own-run-dir","at":"2026-05-25T04:30:01-04:00","actor":{"type":"agent","name":"timothy.shee"},"type":"DecisionRecorded","status":"planning","payload":{"decision_id":"DR-005","decision":"No new schema fields in `schemas/run-metadata.yaml`.","rationale":"The existing `target.worktree.path` + `target.worktree.created` already carry the information we need. The board's `source` field is in-memory only.","alternatives_considered":"Add a `run_dir_root` field; add a `runs_in_worktree: bool` flag.","why_not_alternatives":"Derivable from existing fields. Schema is sacred.","source_artifact":"plan.md"}}
{"schema_version":1,"seq":21,"event_id":"evt_20260525_043001_0021","run_id":"2026-05-25-each-worktree-owns-its-own-run-dir","at":"2026-05-25T04:30:01-04:00","actor":{"type":"agent","name":"timothy.shee"},"type":"DecisionRecorded","status":"planning","payload":{"decision_id":"DR-006","decision":"The pre-merge commit message is `runs: <run_id> (complete)` for completed runs and `abandon: <run_id> (run dir archived)` for abandoned runs.","rationale":"Searchable; consistent with existing convention (`runs: <id>` family of commit messages in the LOG).","alternatives_considered":"A single shared format; descriptive prose; an empty message.","why_not_alternatives":"Differentiating complete/abandon helps grepping history. Prose drifts. Empty messages are noise.","source_artifact":"plan.md"}}
{"schema_version":1,"seq":22,"event_id":"evt_20260525_043001_0022","run_id":"2026-05-25-each-worktree-owns-its-own-run-dir","at":"2026-05-25T04:30:01-04:00","actor":{"type":"agent","name":"timothy.shee"},"type":"DecisionRecorded","status":"planning","payload":{"decision_id":"DR-007","decision":"Board watchdog stays on a single `cfg.runs_path` observer + 1Hz fallback timer. Worktree-side watch roots are not added in V1.","rationale":"Build complexity vs. user pain trade-off \u2014 1Hz fallback gives ~1s latency on cross-worktree file changes, which is fine.","alternatives_considered":"Dynamic multi-watcher (add/remove observers as worktrees come and go); add at startup but never refresh.","why_not_alternatives":"Dynamic is complex. Startup-only misses new runs created mid-session.","source_artifact":"plan.md"}}
